description: No invented facts in any resume, cover letter, or form answer
alwaysApply: true
---

# Truth first

The fact bank is the only source of claims:
`profile/work.yaml`, `profile/projects.yaml`, `profile/education.yaml`, `profile/opentug_brief.md`.

- Reword freely. Never add a number, skill, tool, employer, title, or date that the cited fact does not contain.
- Facts with `status: needs_review` are blocked until Harshal confirms them.
- `claim: analyzed` facts use "analyzed," "traced," or "designed." Never "shipped" or "built."
- `claim: co_shipped` facts say "with the team."
- Project skills (PyTorch, Airflow) may appear in Projects and Skills. Never inside a work bullet.
- Job titles come from `work.yaml` verbatim. OpenTug is "Data Scientist" on every packet, even for Analytics Engineer postings. The headline describes skills ("Analytics Engineering · dbt · Snowflake · Sigma"), never a job title.
- Total experience is about 18 months. Never "3+ years," "senior," or "led a team."
- Indus Novateur is not an employer. It never appears anywhere.
- Never write customer names, voyage IDs, dollar amounts, schema names, or coworker names.
- Visa, salary, location, and EEO answers come only from `profile/answers.yaml`. A `null` there means the job goes to the manual queue.

```yaml
# ❌ rejected: number and skill not in otug-ais
- source: otug-ais
  text: Trained a PyTorch model on 1B+ AIS records

# ✅ accepted: reworded, same facts
- source: otug-ais
  text: Matched 97% of vessel dwells to known terminals using H3 geofences, built with the team
```

When Harshal shares a new fact, add it with the `add-fact` skill. Do not slip it straight into a packet.
